# Manifest and Documentation Maintenance

This rule governs how agents keep project tracking documents current.

## Single Source of Truth

`docs/tasks/manifest.yaml` is the authoritative record of phase and task status.
Other documents (README.md, AGENTS.md, PROJECT-STATUS.md) reference the manifest
rather than duplicating status information.

## After Completing a Phase or Task

1. Update the corresponding entry in `docs/tasks/manifest.yaml`:
   - Set `status: done`
   - Add or update `notes:` with a brief summary of what was built
   - Update the `Last updated` date at the top of the file
2. If the work introduced a new architectural decision, add a numbered ADR to
   `docs/research/architecture-decisions.md`.
3. If the work created new source packages or significantly changed the project
   structure, update the Architecture section of `AGENTS.md`.

## After Adding New Work Items

When discussion produces new features, phases, or deferred items:

1. Add a phase or task entry to `manifest.yaml` with the appropriate status
   (`not_started`, `deferred`, etc.).
2. If a design decision was made, write an ADR.
3. If the phase is ready for implementation, create a task file at
   `docs/tasks/phase-{id}-{name}.md` following the existing format (Goal,
   Context, Files to Read, What to Build, Tests, Acceptance Criteria, Agent
   Prompt).

## At the Start of a New Session

Read `docs/PROJECT-STATUS.md` for a quick orientation. It points to the manifest,
ADRs, and active task files. Check `manifest.yaml` for current status rather than
assuming anything is done or not done.

## Never Duplicate Status

Do not copy phase status into README.md, AGENTS.md, or other docs. Those files
should say "see manifest.yaml for current status" and link to it. This prevents
the staleness that occurs when status lives in multiple places.
